  "id": "conflict-resolution",
  "term": "conflict resolution",
  "definition": "Conflict resolution, in this psychology context, means the executive-function process of handling cognitive conflict so a person can process competing information and choose an appropriate response. It is described as a key part of executive function and involves both information processing and response selection.",
